2. End-to-End Pipeline Hierarchy
The data flow and processing hierarchy from ingestion to user output follows this structured sequence:

Stage A: Data Ingestion & Conversion
Web Scraping: Automated extraction using Playwright to download official scheme PDFs, documents, and web pages.

Multimodal Parsing: Processing complex documents with vision-enabled language models to convert unstructured layouts into clean text.

Storage Routing: Storing raw files and processed text into respective State (Tamil Nadu) and Central board folders.

Stage B: Text Processing & Embedding
Text Splitting: Utilizing LangChain's RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter to break down documents into manageable chunks.

Embedding Generation: Converting text chunks into meaningful mathematical vectors using OpenAI embedding models (GPT-4 / text-embedding models).

Vector Indexing: Storing embeddings in local serverless vector databases (FAISS) segregated into state and central directories.

Stage C: Retrieval & Generation (RAG)
Advanced Retrieval: Implementing Self-RAG combined with Re-Rank mechanisms via LangChain structures.

Prompt Engineering: Applying ToT (Tree of Thoughts) or RTCFR frameworks within system prompts to extract and synthesize information across sources.

Engine & Interface: Utilizing OpenAI models for text generation, deployed via a Streamlit chat interface supporting language and jurisdiction preference routing.


1. System Prompt Design Framework
Your system prompt should enforce accuracy, source attribution, and structured reasoning using the frameworks you selected.

Prompt Architecture Frameworks:

ToT (Tree of Thoughts) / RTCFR Framework: Guides the model to explore multiple reasoning paths (e.g., verifying eligibility rules step-by-step) before finalizing its output.

Core System Prompt Directives:

Role: Act as an expert agricultural schemes and subsidy advisor for Tamil Nadu and Central Government policies.

Constraint 1 (Grounding): Answer exclusively using the retrieved context provided by the RAG vector store. If the information is not present, explicitly state that details are unavailable.

Constraint 2 (Attribution): Always cite the specific government scheme name, document source, or G.O. reference.

Constraint 3 (Language Matching): If the user selected Tamil, respond in fluent, natural Tamil using proper agricultural terminology. If English, respond in professional English.

2. LLM Engine Configuration
Primary Engine Model: OpenAI model (such as GPT-4o or GPT-4 Omni series) for both text generation and multimodal document processing.

Embedding Model: OpenAI embedding endpoint optimized for generating mathematical vector representations of text chunks.

Invocation Structure: Built using LangChain runnables or chains, connecting the retriever, prompt template, and LLM together.

